{
  "summary":"Requests to the Service are failing even though the Pods are in Running phase and appear healthy.",
  "likely_cause":"The Service proxy layer (kube‑proxy) is likely mis‑configured or not functioning correctly, possibly due to an incorrect hairpin‑mode setting that prevents Pods from reaching the Service IP.",
  "confidence":"medium",
  "next_action":"1. From a Pod, bypass the Service and query each endpoint directly (e.g., `wget -qO- 10.244.0.x:9376`) to confirm the Pods serve traffic. 2. Verify kube‑proxy is running on the nodes and inspect its logs for errors. 3. Check the kubelet `--hairpin-mode` flag; ensure it is set to `hairpin-veth` or `promiscuous-bridge`. 4. If hairpin‑mode is incorrect, update the kubelet configuration and restart the kubelet. 5. After fixing, retest the Service request flow."
}
